      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you've found a new kind of silence, one that's heavy and suffocating instead of peaceful. That feeling of being trapped is so real, and the idea of losing everything feels like a massive, impossible hurdle. Maybe the quiet you're seeking isn't found by building walls, but by letting the pressure just release, one small, manageable way. There are ways to make the room feel bigger, even if it's just by making a tiny, deliberate change.",
